WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.615
Say you want to log every call your service makes to its FX quotes client.

2
00:00:07.615 --> 00:00:12.928
A wrapper written by hand repeats the same log-and-forward code in every method.

3
00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:17.312
Forty methods on six interfaces is tedious, and easy to get wrong.

4
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.700
The JDK can write that wrapper for you, while the program runs.

5
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.167
You write one handler.

6
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.473
Here is one call.

7
00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:30.040
Your code calls quoteMicros on what it thinks is an FxQuotes.

8
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:35.356
The object is really a proxy, an instance of a class the JDK generated.

9
00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:40.957
The generated method takes the Method object for quoteMicros, which it looked up once.

10
00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:45.406
It copies the arguments into a new Object array, boxing any primitives.

11
00:00:45.406 --> 00:00:47.725
Then it calls invoke on your handler.

12
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.820
An InvocationHandler has one method, invoke.

13
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:57.257
It gets the proxy, the Method and the arguments, for every call on every method of the interface.

14
00:00:57.867 --> 00:01:00.075
Your handler decides what happens.

15
00:01:00.075 --> 00:01:04.621
This one logs the call, then calls the same method on the real target.

16
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:07.104
The answer comes back as an Object.

17
00:01:07.104 --> 00:01:12.164
The proxy casts it to Long and unboxes it, and the caller gets its plain long.

18
00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:16.252
A handler doesn't have to call a target at all.

19
00:01:16.252 --> 00:01:19.725
In this section's demo there is no target.

20
00:01:19.725 --> 00:01:23.032
The handler returns 1,084,250 by itself.

21
00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:27.773
The proxy class is real, and you can ask it about itself.

22
00:01:27.773 --> 00:01:34.201
It is final, it extends Proxy, and it implements exactly the interfaces you passed, in that order.

23
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.224
It keeps one static Method field per method, looked up once.

24
00:01:38.224 --> 00:01:41.539
The name and the module are details that may change.

25
00:01:42.433 --> 00:01:49.676
To get one, call Proxy.newProxyInstance with a class loader, the list of interfaces, and the handler.

26
00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:56.057
From Kotlin it is the same call, because a Kotlin interface is an ordinary JVM interface.

27
00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.356
Here is a check.

28
00:01:57.356 --> 00:02:00.216
Your handler returns null for quoteMicros.

29
00:02:00.216 --> 00:02:01.919
What does the caller get?

30
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:08.403
A NullPointerException, thrown at the step where the proxy unboxes the answer to a long.
